# USGS us6000t7zp, Mw 7.5, 2026-06-24T22:05:04.053 UTC,
# hypocenter -67.2205 E / 10.5955 N, depth
# 10 km -- the EASTERN, larger event of the doublet
# (the western Mw 7.2, us6000t7zc, is the frame origin).
# In the mesh frame: x = 146084.4 m, z = 25344.4 m.
#
# Mxx / Mzz / Mxz are the horizontal part of the W-phase moment tensor,
# normalized by M0; for this nearly E-W right-lateral mechanism that is
# almost pure Mxz, as it should be in map view.
#
# factor = M0_2D = dtau (M0_3D/dtau)^(2/3)
#        = 5.128e+15 N   (dtau = 3 MPa)
# A 2D source is a line source in 3D and radiates cylindrically, so the 3D
# scalar moment 2.120e+20 N m cannot be used directly. This is the
# approximation quoted in SPECFEM2D's own set_source_parameters.f90.
# Naive alternative, M0_3D / W with W = 20 km:
# 1.060e+16 N, about 2x larger.
#
# NOTE the STF: a Gaussian at f0 = 0.2 Hz is a few seconds long,
# while the real sequence released its moment over 117 s.
# The synthetic moment RATE is therefore far higher than the real one, and
# absolute amplitudes here are NOT comparable with the recordings. The point
# of this run is the geometry, the travel times and the run cost.
